Legal risk is the *potential for litigation to create uncertainty for a firm.* In the context of a two-way financial transaction, an example of legal risk is one party suing the other party in an attempt to terminate the transaction.

In practice it is very close to #voir("regulatory-risk"). 

They are highly integrated with both #voir("operational-risk") and #voir("reputation-risk"). 